## Compiler Stage Timing Breakdown (`samples/iyi/hello.iyi`) (§13)

Measured with existing `--stats` progress tracker across default mode and cached-hit modes (normal vs `IYI_WARM=1` preanalysed prelude):

| Stage | Default Build | Cached Hit (Normal Prelude) | Cached Hit (Preanalysed `IYI_WARM=1`) | Proof |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Parse                            | 0.000s        | 0.000s                      | 0.000s                                | phase=hit/hit (exit 0/0) |
| Top Level Semantic               | 0.128s        | 0.222s                      | 0.240s                                | phase=hit/hit (exit 0/0) |
| Main Semantic                    | 0.043s        | 0.112s                      | 0.110s                                | phase=hit/hit (exit 0/0) |
| Walk (Stale Reach & Effects)     | —             | 0.009s                      | 0.009s                                | phase=hit/hit (exit 0/0) |
| Hashing (CallPath & Build Key)   | —             | 0.298s                      | 0.307s                                | phase=hit/hit (exit 0/0) |
| Codegen (crystal)                | 0.029s        | (not run)                   | (not run)                             | phase=hit/hit, no codegen |
| Codegen (bc+obj)                 | 0.072s        | (not run)                   | (not run)                             | phase=hit/hit, no codegen |
| Codegen (linking)                | 0.042s        | (not run)                   | (not run)                             | phase=hit/hit, no codegen |

*Honest accounting: No speedup is promised (§13, §14). Every hit type-checks: parse, top level, main semantic, walk, and hashing run on every check. Checks stop before codegen, eliminating object compilation and linking overhead. Preanalysed prelude (`IYI_WARM=1`) isolates cold prelude analysis from per-program verification.*

Normal prelude proof: exit=0, phase=hit, codegen_lines=0 -> phase hit no codegen
Preanalysed prelude proof: exit=0, phase=hit, codegen_lines=0 -> phase hit no codegen

